# Redesign: "Connect your IBKR account" screen (missing / expired API key)

## Context
Project: `/Users/islootski/Project/my/my_itbr_nokey` (Streamlit IBKR dashboard, a copy
of `my_itbr` with no API key and an empty DB). Work in this copy only.

Screenshot of the current screen: `/Users/islootski/screenshots/Screenshot 2026-09-26 at 17.21.12.png`.
Read it first. It shows the screen a user sees when the Flex credentials are missing,
after clicking "🔑 Enter API key" and typing an invalid Query ID.

The screen works but is not user friendly. The fonts and colours do not help the user,
and the text is long and in the wrong order. Redesign the screen so a non-technical
user can connect their IBKR account in under 2 minutes without reading `.env` docs.

Relevant code (read before changing anything):
- `app.py`: `main()` (credential-missing branch and the `flex.FlexError` branch),
  `render_api_key_entry()`, `_YODLEE_NOTE`, `render_token_expired()`, `render_sidebar()`,
  `_IBKR_TOKEN_PATH`, `st.set_page_config(...)` at the top.
- `config.py`: `ENV_PATH`, `is_real_value()`, `save_env_values()`.
- `tests/test_app_smoke.py`: section "API key entry button" and "token expiry" tests.
- There is NO `.streamlit/config.toml` today, so the app uses Streamlit's default theme.

## Problems to fix (from the screenshot)
1. Blue text on a dark blue box (`st.info` with the Yodlee note). Low contrast and it is
   the longest text on the screen.
2. Two sets of instructions: the yellow warning says "copy `.env.example` to `.env` and
   edit it"; the button does the same job with no file editing. They compete.
3. Wrong order: a paragraph about Yodlee (the key NOT to use) comes before the fields.
4. Validation error is not next to the field. The Query ID field turns red, but the only
   text beside it is "Press Enter to submit form"; the "digits only" message is elsewhere.
5. The primary action does not stand out: "🔑 Enter API key" and "OK" are secondary
   buttons. There is no Cancel.
6. Noise: the sidebar shows full file paths for the DB and backups; the Net Worth
   controls (Range, Split out dividend income) show below the form with no data.
7. Wrong IBKR menu path. The app says "Account Management → Reporting → Flex Web Service".
   The current Client Portal path is **Performance & Reports → Flex Queries → Flex Web
   Service Configuration** (or Menu → Reporting → Flex Queries → Flex Web Service
   Configuration). Fix `_IBKR_TOKEN_PATH` and every text that uses it.

## Facts to use in the text (verified; do not invent others)
- IBKR Flex tokens expire after **6 hours by default**. The user picks the period in the
  "Should Expire After" list, up to 1 year. Tell the user to pick the longest period.
- Generating a new token replaces the old one; the old token stops working.
- The token is shown once in IBKR; the user must copy it immediately.
- "Valid For IP Address" is optional; blank means no IP restriction.
- The token is a long number; the Flex Query ID is a short number (e.g. 1537307).
- "Yodlee" in IBKR is an entry under Performance & Reports → Third-Party Reports →
  Third-Party Services. It issues a token + query ID for the Yodlee aggregator (Kubera,
  Empower, Snowball). IBKR defines that query, and third-party guides (not IBKR) report
  it carries only base-currency cash balances. This app needs a Flex Web Service token
  plus the user's own Flex Query ID. Do NOT claim whether the Yodlee token string is
  the same as the account's Flex token; that is not verified.
- Error 1012 = token expired, 1015 = token invalid (see `ibkr/flex.py`).

## Target design
One calm card instead of two alert boxes, in this order:
1. Heading: "Connect your IBKR account" (expired case: "Your IBKR token has expired";
   invalid case: "IBKR did not accept your token"). One sentence under it saying the
   data on this computer is safe and Net Worth still works.
2. One primary button: "Connect IBKR account" (expired/invalid: "Enter new token").
3. The button opens a modal with `st.dialog` (title "Connect IBKR", width "medium") that
   contains, top to bottom:
   - Numbered steps (max 4, one line each) to get the token, using the correct menu path
     and the "pick the longest expiry" tip.
   - Field "Flex Web Service token" (`type="password"`, `placeholder`, `help=`), with a
     one-line hint under it: "Use the Flex Web Service token, not the Yodlee token."
   - Field "Flex Query ID" only when the query ID is missing (existing rule), hint
     "Numbers only, e.g. 1537307".
   - Errors shown directly under the field they belong to, in plain words.
   - Buttons: primary "Save and connect", secondary "Cancel".
   - A collapsed `st.expander("Which token do I need?")` with the Yodlee explanation,
     written short (max 4 sentences).
4. After save: success message ("Connected. Loading your data…"), then the normal tabs.
5. Hide the Net Worth controls on this screen when there is no NAV history; show one
   line instead ("Net Worth appears after the first successful refresh").
6. Sidebar: replace full paths with short status ("Database: ready", "Backups: none yet")
   and put the full path in `help=` tooltips.

## Theme (create `.streamlit/config.toml`)
Keys verified with `.venv/bin/streamlit config show` (Streamlit 1.58.0). Use only keys
from that command's output. Relevant keys:
- `[theme]`: `base`, `primaryColor`, `backgroundColor`, `secondaryBackgroundColor`,
  `textColor`, `font`, `headingFont`, `codeFont`, `fontFaces`, `baseFontSize`,
  `baseFontWeight`, `baseRadius`, `buttonRadius`, `borderColor`, `showWidgetBorder`,
  `showSidebarBorder`, `linkColor`, `linkUnderline`.
- Alert colours (this fixes the blue-on-blue box): `blueColor`, `blueBackgroundColor`,
  `blueTextColor`, and the same for `red`, `orange`, `yellow`, `green`, `violet`, `gray`.
- Charts: `chartCategoricalColors`, `chartSequentialColors`, `chartDivergingColors`.
- Sections: `[theme.sidebar]`, `[theme.light]`, `[theme.dark]`, `[theme.light.sidebar]`,
  `[theme.dark.sidebar]`. Define both light and dark so the app follows the OS setting.
Rules:
- One readable sans-serif font for body and headings (e.g. "Inter" from Google Fonts via
  `fontFaces`, or the system font stack). Monospace only for code.
- Every text/background pair must meet WCAG 2.2 AA: 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large
  text and UI borders. Check each pair and list the ratios in your report.
- Gain/loss colours must be colour-blind safe and never rely on colour alone (keep the
  + / − sign).
- Do not remove the existing custom CSS at `app.py` line ~473 unless the theme replaces it.

## Expert roles to apply (review your own work in each role before finishing)
- **Content designer / UX writer:** short labels, one idea per sentence, plain words,
  action-first buttons, errors that say what to do.
- **UI / visual designer:** hierarchy (one primary action per screen), spacing, font,
  palette, consistent button styles.
- **Accessibility reviewer:** WCAG 2.2 AA contrast, keyboard use in the dialog (Tab,
  Enter, Esc), labels on every field, no colour-only meaning.
- **Streamlit developer:** use built-in theme keys and widget parameters (`type=`,
  `help=`, `placeholder=`, `st.dialog`) before any custom CSS.
- **Fintech dashboard UX (optional, for later tabs):** number formats, gains/losses, charts.

