## Claude Code skills and tools to use
- `artifact-design` + Artifact tool: FIRST build a static HTML mockup of the new screen
  (card + open dialog, light and dark) and show it to me. Wait for my OK before coding.
- `dataviz`: palette and chart colour rules for `chartCategoricalColors` etc.
- `caveman:lean-build`: keep scope to this screen, the sidebar status and the theme.
- `run` skill or `claude-in-chrome`: launch the app on port **8502**
  (`.venv/bin/streamlit run app.py --server.port 8502`, never 8501, which the original
  app uses) and take screenshots of: missing-key screen, open dialog, validation error,
  expired-token screen (simulate with a fake token), and success. Light and dark.
- `simplify` then `code-review`: after the change, before reporting.

## Constraints
- Follow `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`: no default parameter values in new or changed
  functions; callers pass every argument as keyword arguments. Existing defaults in
  `config.py` (`Settings` fields, `os.getenv(..., fallback)`) and `prices.fetch_ohlc`:
  do not touch them; list them in the report.
- Never log, print or show the token. Keep the password field.
- Keep `config.save_env_values` as the only writer of `.env`.
- Do not change data loading, parsing, or any other tab.
- `AppTest` support for `st.dialog` is not verified. Check it first with a small test.
  If `AppTest` cannot drive the dialog, keep the form logic in a plain function that the
  dialog calls, and test that function plus the button visibility.

## Tests (required)
- Update the existing "API key entry" and "token expiry" tests to the new texts.
- Button shows on: missing credentials, error 1012, error 1015. Hidden when data loads.
- Query ID field shows only when the query ID is missing.
- Empty token, placeholder token and non-digit query ID are rejected, with the error
  under the right field, and `.env` is not written.
- Save writes `.env` (other lines kept), and the app then shows all six tabs.
- The token value never appears in any rendered element.
- Full suite: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` passes.

